bilities of Data Space Integration and improve their overall data management processes. [Data: Sources (1786, 1787), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 09), (2024, 12, 09))]\n\n## API Management Enhancements\n\nAPI Management has undergone several enhancements, including the introduction of a new API modeling checkbox, security schemes for API artifacts, and support for externalization. These updates are critical for businesses looking to leverage the capabilities of API Management and improve their overall API development processes. [Data: Sources (1788, 1789, 1790), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 09), (2024, 12, 09))]\n\n## Edge Integration Cell Security Updates\n\nThe Edge Integration Cell has undergone several security updates, including the introduction of XML threat protection policy and support for external certificate pinning. These updates are essential for businesses looking to improve their overall security posture and protect their sensitive data. [Data: Sources (1791, 1792, 1793), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 09), (2024, 12, 09))]\n\n## Decentralized Identity Verification Updates\n\nDecentralized Identity Verification has been updated to include support for RC4 release candidate specifications and the addition of credential creation UI form. These updates are critical for businesses looking to leverage the capabilities of Decentralized Identity Verification and improve their overall identity management processes. [Data: Sources (1788, 1789, 1790), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 09), (2024, 12, 09))]\n\n## Connectivity Updates\n\nConnectivity has been updated to include support for new regions, including Australia (Sydney), Brazil (São Paulo), and KSA (Dammam). These updates are essential for businesses looking to leverage the capabilities of Connectivity and improve their overall connectivity processes. [Data: Sources (2031, 2032, 2033), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 28), (2024, 10, 28))]\n\n## Continuous Integration & Delivery Updates\n\nContinuous Integration & Delivery has been updated to include support for bug fixes and improvements to the SAP Fiori for ABAP Platform pipeline. These updates are critical for businesses looking to leverage the capabilities of Continuous Integration & Delivery and improve their overall development processes. [Data: Sources (2032, 2033, 2034), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 28), (2024, 10, 28))]\n\n## SAP Task Center Updates\n\nSAP Task Center has been updated to include improvements to the handling of attachments and support for opening tasks directly via deep links. These updates are essential for businesses looking to leverage the capabilities of SAP Task Center and improve their overall task management processes. [Data: Sources (2036, 2037, 2038), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 28), (2024, 10, 28))]\n\n## Document Management Service Updates\n\nDocument Management Service has been updated to include support for offboarding data and improvements to the migration API. These updates are critical for businesses looking to leverage the capabilities of Document Management Service and improve their overall document management processes. [Data: Sources (101, 102, 103), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2025, 09, 16))]", "# Cloud Foundry and SAP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of key components and entities within the Cloud Foundry and SAP technology ecosystem, highlighting their relationships, capabilities, and notable updates. The information is relevant to the technology landscape as of 2024.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Environment and Components\n\nCloud Foundry is a popular cloud platform that supports a wide range of components and services. The platform provides a flexible and scalable environment for deploying and managing applications. The key components of Cloud Foundry include Edge Integration Cell, Region, and Data Space Integration. These components work together to provide a comprehensive platform for application development and deployment. [Data: Sources (2038, 2039, 2040), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 26), (2024, 10, 28))]\n\n## SAP Technology Components and Updates\n\nSAP technology components, such as SAP Datasphere, SAP AI Launchpad, and SAP Task Center, play a crucial role in supporting digital transformation and innovation. The components have undergone significant updates, including the introduction of new features and improvements. These updates have enhanced the capabilities of the components, making them more efficient and effective. [Data: Sources (102, 103, 104), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 15), (2025, 09, 16))]\n\n## Edge Integration Cell and Its Capabilities\n\nEdge Integration Cell is a key component of Cloud Foundry that provides a range of capabilities, including diagnostics, job management, and API artifact creation. The component has undergone significant updates, including the introduction of new actions and features. These updates have enhanced the capabilities of the component, making it more efficient and effective. [Data: Sources (108, 109, 110), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 14), (2025, 09, 14))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of June 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and significant updates as of June 2024. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations during this period.\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Updates\n\nSAP Build Process Automation has introduced several updates as of June 2024, including the ability to update existing SAPUI5 forms and configure step targets for process visibility. These enhancements aim to improve process automation and visibility, enabling users to track instances specific to their responsibilities. The updates are part of SAP's efforts to streamline process management and enhance user experience. [Data: Sources (2758, 2759), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 17), (2024, 06, 19))]\n\n## Edge Integration Cell Enhancements\n\nThe Edge Integration Cell has undergone significant enhancements as of June 2024, including the ability to route outgoing connections through a proxy, validate incoming request messages against OpenAPI 3.0 specifications, and deploy Kubernetes clusters on Red Hat OpenShift. These updates aim to improve integration capabilities, enhance security, and expand deployment options. The enhancements demonstrate SAP's commitment to innovation and operational efficiency. [Data: Sources (2755, 2756, 2757, 2758), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 17), (2024, 06, 19))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nCloud Identity Services has introduced the SAP Ariba Category Management connector, enabling identity provisioning for SAP Ariba Category Management. This update aims to improve identity management and provisioning capabilities, ensuring seamless integration with SAP Ariba. The connector is part of SAP's efforts to enhance identity and access management. [Data: Sources (2760, 2741), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 17), (2024, 06, 20))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's technology landscape, highlighting key components, their environments, and recent updates. The information is relevant to SAP's operations and development around 2024.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Operational Scope\n\nThe Cloud Identity Services component at SAP plays a pivotal role in managing identities and access control. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2024, helps safeguard SAP against potential security risks and ensures continuous compliance with evolving security standards. Effective identity management not only prevents security breaches but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (545, 731), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 06, 20))]\n\n## Pricing Service Updates\n\nThe Pricing Service component at SAP has undergone several updates in 2024, addressing issues related to engine traces and calculation accuracy. These updates have improved the overall performance and reliability of the Pricing Service, ensuring that it continues to meet the company's operational needs. [Data: Sources (546, 3520), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 06, 19))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Enhancements\n\nThe Kyma Runtime component at SAP has received several enhancements in 2024, including the addition of new provisioning parameters and support for the SAP Ariba Category Management connector. These updates have improved the overall functionality and flexibility of the Kyma Runtime, enabling SAP to better manage its cloud infrastructure and applications. [Data: Sources (545, 2743), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 06, 20))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of December 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technology components, highlighting their core attributes, connections, and noteworthy claims. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations around December 2024.\n\n## SAP Task Center Improvements\n\nThe SAP Task Center has undergone improvements in error messaging for Identity_Authentication_Connectivity_IDS to provide more clarity when the destination contains invalid properties or values. Additionally, the accuracy of the count displayed on the Adapt Filters button in the Web app has been enhanced. These updates aim to improve user experience and efficiency in task management. [Data: Sources (360, 361), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 19), (2024, 12, 19))]\n\n## Decentralized Identity Verification Enhancements\n\nDecentralized Identity Verification has introduced new features, including the ability to create and delete tenants using the administration dashboard. Additionally, verifiable credentials can now be signed with an embedded proof in addition to the existing JSON Web Token (JWT). These enhancements aim to improve identity verification and management processes. [Data: Sources (363, 364), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 18))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nCloud Identity Services have undergone several updates, including the ability to create and edit application-specific groups, download created entities for a provisioning job, and configure access to groups via authorizations based on policies. These updates aim to improve identity management and governance processes. [Data: Sources (366, 367), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 17), (2024, 12, 17))]\n\n## Continuous Integration & Delivery Enhancements\n\nContinuous Integration & Delivery has introduced new features, including the ability to choose from additional Google Cloud Platform regions and Microsoft Azure regions for the SAP BTP ABAP environment. Additionally, SAP Continuous Integration and Delivery can now be consumed in the Microsoft Azure region Brazil (São Paulo). These updates aim to improve integration and delivery processes. [Data: Sources (369, 370), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 09), (2024, 12, 16))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nKyma Runtime has undergone updates, including the API Gateway module: Update to version 2.10.1, which introduces new features and improvements. These updates aim to enhance runtime performance and efficiency. [Data: Sources (371, 372), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 16), (2024, 12, 16))]", "# Cloud Identity Services and Kyma Runtime Overview as of July 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of the key components and services within the Cloud Identity Services and Kyma Runtime environments, highlighting their relationships, operational scopes, and recent updates. The information is relevant to the company's technology operations around mid-2024.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Operational Scope\n\nCloud Identity Services at the company play a pivotal role in managing user identities, access controls, and authentication processes. Their proactive approach, highlighted in recent updates, helps safeguard the company's technology infrastructure against potential security threats and ensures continuous compliance with evolving regulatory standards. Effective identity management not only prevents security breaches but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes and operational efficiency. [Data: Sources (51, 52, 53), Date_Range ((2024, 07, 01), (2024, 07, 17))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates and Enhancements\n\nKyma Runtime has undergone significant updates and enhancements in recent months, including the update to Istio version 1.22.2 and the Telemetry module to version 1.19.0. These updates bring improvements to logs, metrics, and traces, ensuring better resource utilization and stress reduction on configured backends. The updates also include CRD validation checks for TLS certificates and kubectl list views. [Data: Sources (2598, 2599, 2600), Date_Range ((2024, 07, 01), (2024, 07, 17))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between Cloud Identity Services and Kyma Runtime ensures that identity management strategies are secure, scalable, and compliant with regulatory standards. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating identity management with security and compliance strategies at the company. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (51, 52, 53), Date_Range ((2024, 07, 01), (2024, 07, 17))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and significant updates. The information is relevant to SAP's technology landscape as of 2024.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nCloud Identity Services at SAP has undergone significant updates, including the introduction of a new data center in Saudi Arabia, increased maximum OIDC token validity, and the option to reset user passwords via email. These changes aim to enhance user experience and improve security. Effective implementation of these updates is crucial for maintaining a secure and user-friendly environment for SAP users. [Data: Sources (1983, 1986, 1987), Date_Range ((2024, 11, 05), (2024, 11, 05))]\n\n## Data Attribute Recommendation Service Enhancements\n\nThe Data Attribute Recommendation service has been enhanced with new functionalities, including support for dataset schemas with overlapping features and labels, and the ability to mask during model training. These updates aim to improve the accuracy and efficiency of the service, supporting SAP's data-driven decision-making processes. Effective utilization of these enhancements is crucial for maximizing the service's potential. [Data: Sources (1989, 1990), Date_Range ((2024, 11, 05), (2024, 11, 05))]\n\n## ABAP Environment Updates\n\nThe ABAP Environment at SAP has undergone updates, including the introduction of SAPUI5 version 1.120.9 and the ability to access the Landscape Portal from every region. These changes aim to improve the user experience and enhance the functionality of the environment. Effective implementation of these updates is crucial for maintaining a stable and efficient environment for SAP users. [Data: Sources (3338, 3339), Date_Range ((2024, 03, 06), (2024, 03, 06))]", "# SAP Cloud Identity Services Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP Cloud Identity Services, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2024.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Operational Scope\n\nCloud Identity Services at SAP play a pivotal role in managing identities and access to various SAP systems. Their proactive approach helps safeguard SAP against potential security risks and ensures continuous compliance with evolving security regulations. Effective identity management not only prevents security anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (2591, 2592, 2593), Date_Range ((2024, 07, 17), (2024, 09, 25))]\n\n## Identity Provisioning Capabilities\n\nIdentity Provisioning is a key component of Cloud Identity Services, enabling the creation, management, and deletion of identities across various SAP systems. Its capabilities include supporting OAuth certificate authentication, SAP BTP Platform Members (Cloud Foundry) connector, and Procurement Data Warehouse connector. [Data: Sources (2595, 2597, 2008), Date_Range ((2024, 07, 17), (2024, 10, 31))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between Cloud Identity Services and other SAP departments, such as SAP BTP Platform Members (Cloud Foundry) and Procurement Data Warehouse, ensures that identity management strategies are aligned with regulatory requirements. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP. [Data: Sources (2592, 2597, 2008), Date_Range ((2024, 07, 17), (2024, 10, 31))]", "# SAP Cloud Identity Services and Technology Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's Cloud Identity Services and related technologies, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates as of 2025. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations and development around this time.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Operational Scope\n\nCloud Identity Services at SAP play a pivotal role in managing identities and access across various environments. Their proactive approach ensures continuous compliance with evolving security standards and regulations. Effective identity management not only prevents security breaches but also supports SAP's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (56, 1433), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 02, 11))]\n\n## Identity Provisioning and Governance\n\nIdentity Provisioning ensures that all SAP operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on corporate governance and contract management is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex contracts and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (1526), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 01, 29))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between Cloud Identity Services and Identity Provisioning ensures that identity management strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider security risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating identity management with security compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning SAP's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (1527, 1528), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 01, 29))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates and Enhancements\n\nCloud Identity Services have undergone significant updates and enhancements as of 2025, including the introduction of new conditional functions, group mapping changes, and provisioning sub-attributes of emails attributes. These updates aim to improve identity management and access control, ensuring secure and efficient operations. [Data: Sources (1433, 1435), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 02, 11))]\n\n## Deprecation of SAP Ariba Category Management Connector\n\nThe SAP Ariba Category Management connector has been deprecated as of 2025, due to an update of the business solution's local user store, which no longer requires user provisioning jobs. This change aims to simplify identity management and access control, reducing the risk of security breaches. [Data: Sources (192, 193), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 27), (2025, 08, 27))]\n\n## New Conditional Functions and Group Mapping Changes\n\nNew conditional functions and group mapping changes have been introduced in Cloud Identity Services as of 2025, enabling more efficient and secure identity management and access control. These updates aim to improve the overall security posture of SAP's technology operations. [Data: Sources (1520, 1521), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 01, 29))]", "# Cloud Identity Services and Technology Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into the key components of SAP's Cloud Identity Services and Technology, highlighting their interactions and updates within the organizational framework to ensure effective identity management and technological advancements. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2025.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Operational Scope\n\nThe Cloud Identity Services at SAP play a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating identity risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP against potential identity pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving identity regulations. Effective identity management not only prevents identity anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (1, 2), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 02, 25))]\n\n## Identity Provisioning and Governance\n\nThe Identity Provisioning Department ensures that all SAP's operations adhere to the identity standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on identity governance and management, noted starting 2025, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex identities and agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high identity standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (3), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 02, 25))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Identity Management\n\nCollaboration between the Cloud Identity Services and Identity Provisioning Departments, established in 2025, ensures that identity management strategies are effective and compliant. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating identity management with technological advancements at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (4, 5), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 02, 25))]\n\n## Technological Advancements and Integration\n\nThe integration of Cloud Identity Services with other technological components, such as SAP Cloud ALM and SAP S/4 HANA Cloud, has enabled seamless identity management and technological advancements. This integration has improved the overall efficiency and effectiveness of SAP's operations, ensuring that the company remains competitive in the market. [Data: Sources (6, 7), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 02, 25))]\n\n## User Management and Identity Types\n\nThe introduction of new user types, such as Alumni, has enabled SAP to manage its user base more effectively. This has improved the overall user experience and has enabled SAP to better manage its identity management processes. [Data: Source (8), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 02, 25))]\n\n## Graph and Business Data Management\n\nThe ability to edit business data graphs in JSON format has improved the overall efficiency and effectiveness of SAP's operations. This has enabled SAP to better manage its business data and has improved the overall user experience. [Data: Source (9), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 02, 25))]", "# SAP Cloud Identity Services Overview as of May 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP's Cloud Identity Services, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations around May 2025.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Operational Scope\n\nCloud Identity Services at SAP play a pivotal role in managing identity and access within the company's technology framework. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP against potential security pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving regulatory standards. Effective identity management not only prevents security anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (921, 922, 923), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 05, 08))]\n\n## Regular Upgrade and New Features\n\nCloud Identity Services have been upgraded, introducing new features such as the ability to download and view deleted entities for a provisioning job, manage corporate identity providers, and return termsOfUse and privacyPolicy parameters. These updates underscore the commitment to upholding high security standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (924, 925, 926), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 05, 08))]\n\n## Support for SAP Extension Schema\n\nCloud Identity Services support the SAP extension schema for groups, including application ID, type, and supported operations. This custom SCIM schema extension is defined by SAP's Organizational Data Model (ODM) and is used to enrich the standard SCIM User resource with SAP-specific attributes. [Data: Sources (927, 928, 929), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 05, 08))]", "# SAP Cloud Identity Services Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP's Cloud Identity Services, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to SAP's operations around 2025.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Operational Scope\n\nCloud Identity Services at SAP play a pivotal role in managing identities, access, and authentication across various environments. Their proactive approach helps safeguard SAP against potential security pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving security regulations. Effective identity management not only prevents security anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (1, 2), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 08), (2025, 05, 08))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between various departments, including Cloud Identity Services, ensures that security and compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with security compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (3, 4), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 08), (2025, 05, 08))]\n\n## Regular Upgrades and Enhancements\n\nCloud Identity Services have been upgraded regularly, with the latest upgrade occurring in 2025. These upgrades have brought various enhancements, including improved security features, better performance, and increased scalability. The upgrades have been instrumental in maintaining SAP's operational stability and ensuring continuous compliance with evolving security regulations. [Data: Sources (5, 6), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 08), (2025, 05, 08))]", "# Cloud Identity Services Overview as of June 2025\n\nThis report delves into the key components and features of Cloud Identity Services, highlighting their operational scope, core attributes, connections, and noteworthy claims. The information is relevant to the company's operations around mid-2025.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Operational Scope\n\nCloud Identity Services at SAP play a pivotal role in managing user identities and ensuring regulatory compliance. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP against potential identity-related pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving regulatory standards. Effective identity management not only prevents identity anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (1, 2), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 06, 04))]\n\n## Regular Upgrades and Enhancements\n\nCloud Identity Services have been upgraded regularly, with the latest upgrade occurring in June 2025. These upgrades have introduced new features and enhancements, such as support for new